<title>USA: Airport manager gives workers resignation forms.</title>
<headline>Airport manager gives workers resignation forms.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Jacksonville, Fla., airport manager handed nine supervisors blank resignation forms in a meeting, implying that the supervisors should quit if they could not work as a team to resolve staffing problems, the FAA acknowledged Wednesday in response to a news release sent by two airport workers' groups.</p>
<p>The National Air Traffic Controllers Association and the Professional Airways Systems Specialists in a written statement called the act &quot;appalling&quot; and said the workers who had lodged the complaints were being &quot;harrassed.&quot;</p>
